---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/services/ServiceHero.astro';
import MeasurementArchitectureBuilder from '../../components/services/MeasurementArchitectureBuilder.astro';
import ServiceCTA from '../../components/services/ServiceCTA.astro';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
---
<BaseLayout title="Measurement Planning & Architecture Design | Upsight Digital" description="Design the measurement architecture before implementation, including KPIs, event taxonomy, data flows, identity, source systems, platforms, integrations, dependencies, ownership and implementation roadmap." canonical="https://upsight.digital/services/measurement-planning/" jsonLd={serviceSchema('Measurement Planning & Architecture Design', 'Measurement system design covering KPIs, event and identity architecture, data flows, integrations, dependencies, ownership, privacy requirements and implementation roadmap.', '/services/measurement-planning/')}>
  <ServiceHero eyebrow="MEASUREMENT ARCHITECTURE" title="Measurement Planning &amp; Architecture Design" lead="Design the measurement system before anyone starts adding tags, SDKs or APIs." detail="Upsight turns business requirements into an implementation-ready blueprint covering KPIs, events, identities, data sources, collection paths, integrations, destinations, privacy requirements, ownership and rollout phases." primaryLabel="Design My Measurement Architecture"><div slot="visual" class="rounded-xl border border-primary/30 bg-card p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-7"><p class="text-primary">BUSINESS JOURNEYS → EVENT &amp; KPI MODEL</p><p class="mt-2">SOURCES · Website · App · Backend / CRM · Calls / Forms</p><p class="text-primary">↓</p><p>COLLECTION · Data Layer / GTM · SDK · API · Server Events</p><p class="text-primary">↓</p><p>PROCESSING · sGTM · CDP · Warehouse · Custom Logic</p><p class="text-primary">↓</p><p>DESTINATIONS · Analytics · MMP · Advertising · BI</p></div></ServiceHero>
  <div class="container py-10 md:py-16"><MeasurementArchitectureBuilder /></div>
  <section class="bg-muted/30 py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">ARCHITECTURE DELIVERABLES</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">What a Measurement Architecture Actually Defines</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{[['Business and KPI framework','Objectives, questions, KPI definitions, calculation logic and source of truth.'],['Journey and event model','User journeys, conversion points, event names, parameters and lifecycle states.'],['Identity architecture','Anonymous, authenticated, transaction, campaign, device and CRM identifiers with clear rules.'],['Data-flow architecture','Sources, browser/app/server collection, transformations, integrations and destinations.'],['Platform architecture','Relevant analytics, GTM/sGTM, product analytics, MMP, CMP, warehouse, advertising and BI components.'],['Privacy requirements','Consent states, allowed destinations, data minimization and requirements provided by privacy stakeholders.'],['Ownership and governance','Marketing, analytics, development, backend, QA and release responsibilities.'],['Implementation roadmap','Dependencies, phases, technical prerequisites, environments, QA stages and handover.']].map(([h,d])=><article class="service-proof-card"><h3>{h}</h3><p>{d}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">SOURCE OF TRUTH</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Every KPI Needs a Source of Truth</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The measurement event is a representation for analysis and activation. It does not replace the operational record that defines the underlying business outcome.</p><div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border"><table class="w-full min-w-[760px] text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-muted"><tr>{['Metric','Source of truth','Measurement event','Destinations','Validation'].map(x=><th class="p-3 font-semibold">{x}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{[['Order revenue','Backend ordering system','purchase + transaction_id','Analytics · Ads · dashboard','Reconcile event to finalized order'],['Lead status','CRM','lead_status_updated','Analytics · ad platforms · CRM reporting','Compare status changes to CRM record'],['App subscription','Backend or store record','subscription_started / renewed','Product analytics · MMP · BI','Reconcile lifecycle event to subscription state'],['Campaign attribution','MMP / platform signal','attributed install or event','MMP · partners · reporting','Compare using stated attribution rules']].map(row=><tr class="border-t">{row.map(cell=><td class="p-3 align-top">{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="bg-muted/30 py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">CONNECTION SPECIFICATION</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Document Every Important Connection</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Each connection describes what triggers it, what data crosses the boundary, where it goes, who owns it and how the team verifies delivery.</p><article class="mt-6 rounded-xl border bg-card p-6"><p class="service-kicker">SAMPLE CONNECTION</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">Backend → Server Measurement Layer</h3><dl class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">{[['Trigger','Order finalized'],['Payload','order_id, revenue, currency, products and approved account identifier'],['Destinations','Analytics, advertising and reporting as specified'],['Owner','Backend development with analytics implementation'],['QA','Compare source order to the downstream event payload']].map(([h,d])=><div><dt class="font-semibold">{h}</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{d}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Illustrative specification, not a client implementation.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">SOLUTION OPTIONS</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Architecture Is a Design Decision, Not a Tool List</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Direct platform integrations, a server-side routing layer and a warehouse-centered model solve different problems. Selection depends on control needs, data ownership, capacity, reporting requirements and maintenance constraints.</p><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">{[['Direct platform integrations','Effort: lower initial complexity for a small number of destinations. Control: platform-specific. Dependency: more tied to each vendor integration.'],['Server-side routing layer','Effort: infrastructure and routing setup. Control: centralized transformations and delivery. Maintenance: hosting, consent, access and destination changes.'],['Warehouse-centered model','Effort: data modeling and pipeline work. Ownership: more centralized raw/normalized data. Reporting flexibility: high when governance and skills support it.']].map(([h,d])=><article class="service-proof-card"><h3>{h}</h3><p>{d}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="bg-muted/30 py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">DELIVERY ROADMAP</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Plan the Work in Dependent Phases</h2><ol class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-5">{[['01 · Measurement Model','KPIs · journeys · events · identifiers'],['02 · Data Collection','dataLayer · SDKs · APIs · backend events'],['03 · Platform Integrations','analytics · MMP · ads · consent · server-side'],['04 · Validation','QA · reconciliation · edge cases'],['05 · Governance','documentation · ownership · release process · monitoring']].map(([h,d],i)=><li class="service-proof-card"><p class="service-kicker">PHASE {i+1}</p><h3 class="mt-2">{h.slice(5)}</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm">{d}</p>{i<4&&<p class="mt-3 text-primary" aria-label="follows prior phase">↓ next phase</p>}</li>)}</ol><p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground">The sequence and dependencies are illustrative. A project plan should reflect team availability, system readiness and release constraints.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">EXAMPLE OWNERSHIP</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Make Responsibilities Visible</h2><div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border"><table class="w-full min-w-[700px] text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-muted"><tr>{['Workstream','Upsight','Client dev','Marketing','Privacy'].map(x=><th class="p-3 font-semibold">{x}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{[['Measurement model','Lead','Input','Input','Input'],['Data layer / SDK spec','Lead','Build','Input',''],['Platform configuration','Lead','Support','Input',''],['Backend integration','Design','Build','',''],['Consent requirements','Implement','Support','','Approve'],['QA / validation','Lead','Support','Support',''],['Production release','','Deploy','Support',''],['Documentation','Lead','Input','Input','']].map(row=><tr class="border-t">{row.map(cell=><td class="p-3">{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Illustrative responsibility model; project roles vary.</p></div></section>
  <section class="bg-muted/30 py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><p class="service-kicker">TECHNOLOGY INDEPENDENCE</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-3">Design Around the Measurement Problem</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-muted-foreground">We map the required events, identities, data ownership, integrations and operating constraints before recommending a tool path. An architecture may include GA4/GTM, Firebase, Amplitude, Mixpanel, PostHog, AppsFlyer, Adjust, Branch, Kochava, server-side GTM, BigQuery, Snowflake, CMPs, advertising platforms, CRM/backend systems or custom APIs, where relevant.</p><h2 class="service-heading mt-10">When Architecture Design Helps</h2><ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{['New analytics implementation','Mobile app launch','MMP selection or migration','Server-side migration','Multi-market measurement','New CMP or privacy architecture','Fragmented vendor stack','Offline and online conversion journeys','Analytics replatforming','Enterprise implementation across development teams'].map(item=><li class="rounded-lg border bg-card p-3 text-sm">{item}</li>)}</ul><p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground">This work connects to <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/ga4-gtm-setup/">GA4/GTM Setup</a>, <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/mobile-analytics/">Mobile Analytics</a>, <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/mobile-measurement/">Mobile Measurement</a>, <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/server-side-tracking/">Server-Side Tracking</a>, <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/cookie-consent/">Cookie Consent &amp; CMP</a> and <a class="text-primary underline" href="/services/analytics-dashboards/">Analytics Dashboards</a>.</p></div></section>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16"><div class="container"><h2 class="service-heading">Common Questions</h2><div class="mt-5 grid gap-3">{[['What is a measurement plan?','A measurement plan defines the business questions, KPIs, event model, sources, collection rules, destinations and validation criteria needed to produce useful, governed data.'],['How is this different from GA4/GTM implementation?','Architecture work defines how systems, identities, data flows and owners fit together. GA4/GTM implementation configures the website measurement layer within that design.'],['Do we need architecture design before implementation?','It is most useful when several sources, platforms, teams or privacy requirements interact. Small, contained changes may need only a focused specification.'],['Can you work with our existing technology stack?','Yes. Planning starts by documenting current systems and constraints, then identifying changes or connections the requirements call for.'],['Can you compare vendors and provide developer-ready specifications?','We can compare options against agreed requirements and document events, payloads, dependencies, owners and validation steps.'],['Can you design web, app and backend measurement together?','Yes. The architecture can map browser, app and backend sources together, with platform-specific collection and privacy rules clearly defined.'],['Can you review another vendor’s architecture or phase a large implementation?','A review can assess flows, assumptions, dependencies, ownership and testability. A phased roadmap can then sequence work around system readiness and team capacity.']].map(([q,a])=><details class="rounded-lg border bg-card p-4"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">{q}</summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">{a}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
  <ServiceCTA title="Turn measurement requirements into an implementation blueprint." detail="Map the systems, data flows, dependencies and ownership before implementation begins." primaryLabel="Design My Measurement Architecture" />
</BaseLayout>
